{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/postHog(projectToken:host:plan:backoff:clock:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":") for your PostHog project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token and the host, posts to the host’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\/batch\/"},{"text":" with a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splits each batch to PostHog’s limits (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"). A batch with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record the encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"5xx, 408 and 429, and drops and reports any other status. The project token goes in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the body, so no header field is needed, and no trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"text":" leaves","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an anonymous event. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":" is the record’s session, from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$session_id"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record identifier. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"uuid"},{"text":" is the record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event carries ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$process_person_profile: false"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$geoip_disable: true"},{"text":". The record’s vendor","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and trace context aren’t sent, and the standard context is sent as PostHog’s own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"properties (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_name"},{"text":" and the like).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals, and a property whose name starts with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or is "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is left out and logged. A record the encoder can’t write is left out and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one whose event isn’t "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, and one too large for PostHog’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event limit. The destination reports each as "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason is a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to TraffluentCollector, use "},{"code":"CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"CollectorEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instead."}]},{"code":["import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let postHog = try HTTPDestination.postHog(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    host: postHogHost,  \/\/ https:\/\/us.i.posthog.com, https:\/\/eu.i.posthog.com or your own","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: postHog)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what PostHog receives, and why, in more detail."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEnc